### =========================================================================
### Baseline API — requests.http
### =========================================================================
### Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or JetBrains' built-in
### HTTP Client. Requests are grouped and ordered to form a realistic
### end-to-end flow — run top to bottom the first time so variables like
### {{accessToken}} get populated from real responses along the way.
###
### KNOWN GAP — READ FIRST:
### There is currently no public endpoint to create an Organization. The
### only way to get a first Organization + Owner Membership into the
### database today is via the Django admin or a shell command:
###
###   python manage.py createsuperuser
###   python manage.py shell -c "
###     from apps.core.models import Organization, Membership
###     from apps.accounts.models import User
###     org = Organization.objects.create(name='Acme Inc', slug='acme-inc')
###     user = User.objects.get(email='you@example.com')
###     Membership.objects.create(organization=org, user=user, role='owner', status='active')
###     print(org.id)
###   "
###
### Paste that org id into @orgId below. This file assumes that setup step
### has already been done. If you'd like a real POST /organizations/
### endpoint instead, ask — it wasn't in the confirmed MVP scope.
### =========================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000
@apiV1 = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1

### Fill in after step 1 (register) + step 2 (login) run once.
@accessToken =
@refreshToken =

### Fill in using the setup step above (or after creating one via admin).
@orgId =

### Populated automatically as you run requests further down — copy the
### `id` from each response into the matching variable.
@customerId =
@leadId =
@projectId =
@taskId =
@invoiceId =
@documentId =
@notificationId =
@invitationToken =
@membershipId =


### =========================================================================
### HEALTH CHECK (no auth)
### =========================================================================

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/


### =========================================================================
### AUTH — apps/accounts (prefix: /api/v1/auth/)
### No X-Organization-Id header on any of these — auth happens before a
### tenant workspace is selected.
### =========================================================================

### Register a new user
# @name register
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/register/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner@acme.test",
  "password": "a-very-secure-password-123",
  "first_name": "Ada",
  "last_name": "Owner"
}

### Log in — copy `access` into @accessToken and `refresh` into @refreshToken above
# @name login
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/login/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "owner@acme.test",
  "password": "a-very-secure-password-123"
}

### Refresh the access token
# @name refreshToken
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/token/refresh/
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Current user profile
GET {{apiV1}}/auth/me/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Log out (blacklists the refresh token)
POST {{apiV1}}/auth/logout/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh": "{{refreshToken}}"
}


### =========================================================================
### CORE — memberships, invitations (prefix: /api/v1/)
### Every request below this point needs BOTH headers unless noted:
###   Authorization: Bearer <token>
###   X-Organization-Id: <org uuid>  (re-validated against a live Membership
###                                   on every request — see
###                                   TenantContextMiddleware)
### =========================================================================

### List memberships in the active org
GET {{apiV1}}/memberships/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Retrieve one membership
GET {{apiV1}}/memberships/{{membershipId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Create an invitation (requires invitations:create — Owner/Admin)
# @name createInvitation
POST {{apiV1}}/invitations/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "newmember@acme.test",
  "role": "member"
}

### List invitations
GET {{apiV1}}/invitations/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Revoke an invitation (requires invitations:revoke)
DELETE {{apiV1}}/invitations/{{invitationToken}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Accept an invitation — NO X-Organization-Id (no membership exists yet).
### The invited user must be logged in as themselves first (register/login
### with the invited email), then call this with the token from the
### invitation email / createInvitation response.
POST {{apiV1}}/invitations/accept/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{invitationToken}}"
}


### =========================================================================
### CUSTOMERS — apps/customers (prefix: /api/v1/)
### =========================================================================

### List customers
GET {{apiV1}}/customers/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### List customers — filtered + searched
GET {{apiV1}}/customers/?is_archived=false&search=acme
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Create a customer (requires customers:create)
# @name createCustomer
POST {{apiV1}}/customers/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Acme Retail Ltd",
  "primary_contact_name": "Chidi Okafor",
  "email": "chidi@acmeretail.test",
  "phone": "+2348012345678",
  "billing_address": "12 Marina Road, Lagos",
  "data_source": "direct"
}

### Create a customer sourced from an imported list — consent_obtained_at required
POST {{apiV1}}/customers/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Imported Prospect Co",
  "email": "prospect@example.test",
  "data_source": "imported",
  "consent_obtained_at": "2026-08-01T10:00:00Z"
}

### Retrieve a customer
GET {{apiV1}}/customers/{{customerId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Update a customer (requires customers:update)
PATCH {{apiV1}}/customers/{{customerId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "phone": "+2348099999999"
}

### Archive a customer (ordinary workflow, not NDPA erasure)
PATCH {{apiV1}}/customers/{{customerId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "is_archived": true
}

### Delete a customer (requires customers:delete — real hard-delete, no invoices attached)
DELETE {{apiV1}}/customers/{{customerId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}


### =========================================================================
### LEADS — apps/leads (prefix: /api/v1/)
### =========================================================================

### List leads
GET {{apiV1}}/leads/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### List leads — filtered by status
GET {{apiV1}}/leads/?status=new
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Create a lead (requires leads:create)
# @name createLead
POST {{apiV1}}/leads/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ngozi Balogun",
  "company_name": "Balogun Textiles",
  "email": "ngozi@balogun-textiles.test",
  "phone": "+2347011122233",
  "data_source": "inbound"
}

### Retrieve a lead
GET {{apiV1}}/leads/{{leadId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Update a lead's status (requires leads:update)
PATCH {{apiV1}}/leads/{{leadId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "qualified"
}

### Convert a lead — creates a new Customer (requires leads:convert)
POST {{apiV1}}/leads/{{leadId}}/convert/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Convert a lead — link to an EXISTING customer instead (upsell/expansion case)
POST {{apiV1}}/leads/{{leadId}}/convert/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_id": "{{customerId}}"
}

### Delete a lead (requires leads:delete)
DELETE {{apiV1}}/leads/{{leadId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}


### =========================================================================
### PROJECTS & TASKS — apps/projects (prefix: /api/v1/)
### =========================================================================

### List projects
GET {{apiV1}}/projects/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### List projects — filtered by status/customer
GET {{apiV1}}/projects/?status=active&customer={{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Create a client project (requires projects:create — also entitlement-checked)
# @name createProject
POST {{apiV1}}/projects/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Acme Website Redesign",
  "description": "Full redesign + CMS migration",
  "status": "planning",
  "customer": "{{customerId}}",
  "start_date": "2026-09-01",
  "due_date": "2026-11-30"
}

### Create an INTERNAL project — no customer (confirmed: Project.customer is optional)
POST {{apiV1}}/projects/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Internal: Q3 Hiring Plan",
  "status": "planning"
}

### Retrieve a project (detail view includes nested tasks)
GET {{apiV1}}/projects/{{projectId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Update a project (requires projects:update)
PATCH {{apiV1}}/projects/{{projectId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "active"
}

### Delete a project (requires projects:delete)
DELETE {{apiV1}}/projects/{{projectId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### ---- Tasks ----

### List tasks
GET {{apiV1}}/tasks/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### List tasks — filtered by project/assignee/status
GET {{apiV1}}/tasks/?project={{projectId}}&status=todo
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Create a task inside a project (requires tasks:create)
# @name createTask
POST {{apiV1}}/tasks/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "project": "{{projectId}}",
  "title": "Design homepage wireframes",
  "description": "Low-fidelity wireframes for review",
  "priority": "high",
  "due_date": "2026-09-10"
}

### Create a STANDALONE task — no project (confirmed: Task.project is optional)
POST {{apiV1}}/tasks/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Personal reminder: renew domain",
  "priority": "low"
}

### Retrieve a task
GET {{apiV1}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Assign a task — fires a TASK_ASSIGNED notification to the assignee
PATCH {{apiV1}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "assigned_to": "{{membershipId}}",
  "status": "in_progress"
}

### Delete a task (requires tasks:delete)
DELETE {{apiV1}}/tasks/{{taskId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}


### =========================================================================
### INVOICES — apps/invoices (prefix: /api/v1/)
### DELETE is intentionally disabled (405) — invoices are financial
### records; use the void action instead.
### =========================================================================

### List invoices
GET {{apiV1}}/invoices/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### List invoices — filtered by status
GET {{apiV1}}/invoices/?status=sent
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Create an invoice (requires invoices:create — customer is REQUIRED)
# @name createInvoice
POST {{apiV1}}/invoices/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer": "{{customerId}}",
  "project": "{{projectId}}",
  "currency": "NGN",
  "subtotal": "500000.00",
  "tax_amount": "37500.00",
  "issued_at": "2026-08-18",
  "due_date": "2026-09-01",
  "notes": "50% deposit for website redesign"
}

### Retrieve an invoice
GET {{apiV1}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Update an invoice (requires invoices:update)
PATCH {{apiV1}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "sent"
}

### Mark an invoice paid
POST {{apiV1}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/mark_paid/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Void an invoice (requires invoices:void)
POST {{apiV1}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/void/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Attempt delete — expect 405 Method Not Allowed by design
DELETE {{apiV1}}/invoices/{{invoiceId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}


### =========================================================================
### DOCUMENTS — apps/documents (prefix: /api/v1/)
### Upload is multipart/form-data, not JSON — exactly one of
### customer/project/invoice must be set (DB-enforced).
### =========================================================================

### List documents
GET {{apiV1}}/documents/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### List documents — filtered by owner
GET {{apiV1}}/documents/?customer={{customerId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Upload a document attached to a customer (requires documents:create)
### REST Client: point `< ./sample.pdf` at a real local file before running.
POST {{apiV1}}/documents/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=BaselineBoundary

--BaselineBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="customer"

{{customerId}}
--BaselineBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="description"

Signed contract
--BaselineBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="sample.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ./sample.pdf
--BaselineBoundary--

### Retrieve a document
GET {{apiV1}}/documents/{{documentId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Delete a document (requires documents:delete — also removes the underlying file)
DELETE {{apiV1}}/documents/{{documentId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}


### =========================================================================
### NOTIFICATIONS — apps/notifications (prefix: /api/v1/)
### Always scoped to the CALLER's own notifications (recipient=request.user)
### regardless of role — no RBAC gate beyond being authenticated.
### =========================================================================

### List my notifications
GET {{apiV1}}/notifications/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### List unread only
GET {{apiV1}}/notifications/?is_read=false
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Unread count
GET {{apiV1}}/notifications/unread_count/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Retrieve a notification
GET {{apiV1}}/notifications/{{notificationId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Mark one notification read
POST {{apiV1}}/notifications/{{notificationId}}/mark_read/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}

### Mark all read
POST {{apiV1}}/notifications/mark_all_read/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}


### =========================================================================
### ANALYTICS — apps/analytics (prefix: /api/v1/)
### Requires analytics:view (Owner/Admin/Manager, per the seeded RBAC grants)
### =========================================================================

### Dashboard summary — leads, customers, projects, tasks, revenue
GET {{apiV1}}/analytics/dashboard/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgId}}


### =========================================================================
### BILLING — apps/billing (prefix: /api/v1/billing/)
### Webhooks authenticate via HMAC signature, NOT Bearer/X-Organization-Id —
### these are provider-to-server calls, not requests you'd normally send by
### hand. Included for completeness / local signature-verification testing.
### Signature values below are placeholders and WILL fail verification
### unless you compute a real HMAC against your PAYSTACK_WEBHOOK_SECRET /
### OPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET.
### =========================================================================

### Paystack webhook (charge.success)
POST {{apiV1}}/billing/webhooks/paystack/
Content-Type: application/json
X-Paystack-Signature: REPLACE_WITH_REAL_HMAC_SHA512_SIGNATURE

{
  "event": "charge.success",
  "data": {
    "id": "evt_test_001",
    "reference": "ref_test_001",
    "metadata": {
      "organization_id": "{{orgId}}",
      "plan_code": "trial"
    }
  }
}

### Opay webhook (TRANSACTION.SUCCESS)
POST {{apiV1}}/billing/webhooks/opay/
Content-Type: application/json
Signature: REPLACE_WITH_REAL_HMAC_SHA256_SIGNATURE

{
  "type": "TRANSACTION.SUCCESS",
  "data": {
    "orderNo": "order_test_001",
    "metadata": {
      "organization_id": "{{orgId}}",
      "plan_code": "trial"
    }
  }
}


### =========================================================================
### PLATFORM ADMIN — apps/platform_admin (prefix: /api/v1/platform-admin/)
### Requires request.user.is_staff = True — NOT gated by tenant Membership
### role. No X-Organization-Id needed (these views query cross-tenant via
### .unscoped() explicitly). Log in as a superuser/staff account first.
### =========================================================================

### Search organizations
GET {{apiV1}}/platform-admin/organizations/?q=acme
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Organization detail (includes active member count)
GET {{apiV1}}/platform-admin/organizations/{{orgId}}/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Suspend an organization — hard kill-switch, checked on every tenant request
POST {{apiV1}}/platform-admin/organizations/{{orgId}}/suspend/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Unsuspend an organization
POST {{apiV1}}/platform-admin/organizations/{{orgId}}/unsuspend/
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
